Hermes Portable: strict bundled Git Bash and an operator artifact mirror.

pm/shell.py: with HERMES_GIT_BASH_ONLY=1, bash() only returns the staged
PortableGit bash or HERMES_GIT_BASH_PATH. A slow first start (antivirus scan)
no longer falls back to a system Git for Windows or a bash on PATH.

pm/artifact_mirror.py: HERMES_ARTIFACT_MIRROR names an operator mirror of
https://hermes-assets.nousresearch.com (for example a Nexus raw proxy
repository). PM tries <mirror>/upstream/sha256/<sha256> first, then the
locked upstream URL, then the public archive. Every source is still verified
against the locked sha256, so a closed-network build or lazy install can
fetch Python, Node, PortableGit, Chromium, ffmpeg and friends from Nexus.

diff --git a/pm/artifact_mirror.py b/pm/artifact_mirror.py
index 3d3030b8..b673b719 100644
--- a/pm/artifact_mirror.py
+++ b/pm/artifact_mirror.py
@@ -29,4 +29,10 @@ def pinned_source(url: str, dest: Path, sha256: str) -> Source:
     archive = mirror_url(sha256)
     # The lock records registry.npmjs.org; a user's npm mirror serves the same pinned bytes (#123132).
     url = npm_registry_url(url, os.environ)
+    # HERMES_ARTIFACT_MIRROR: an operator mirror of the origin above (e.g. a Nexus raw
+    # proxy) tried first, so closed networks never wait on unreachable upstream hosts.
+    operator = os.environ.get("HERMES_ARTIFACT_MIRROR", "").strip().rstrip("/")
+    if operator:
+        local = f"{operator}/{object_key(sha256)}"
+        return Source(local, dest, sha256, fallbacks=tuple(dict.fromkeys(u for u in (url, archive) if u != local)))
     return Source(url, dest, sha256, fallbacks=() if url == archive else (archive,))
